  "user_scenario": "You are Gretchen Hallstrom, 47, the office manager of a dental practice in Appleton. You speak plainly, a little tiredly, and you like to finish things in one call. On May 12 you had arthroscopic surgery on your right knee at the Riverbend Surgery & Imaging Center in Grand Chute. In July Anthem wrote to you that, after reviewing the surgery, it had decided the surgery was not medically necessary, and in September another letter said Riverbend's appeal of that decision was turned down. Riverbend's patient portal then sent you a form to sign so that Riverbend could file one more appeal in your name. You have decided you do not want another appeal: you are calling to say so and to have this claim settled so that you are never billed for the surgery.\n\nYou open by saying who you are, Gretchen Hallstrom, that you are calling from your cell number 9205550217, and why you are calling: you got the form asking you to sign so Riverbend can appeal your knee surgery claim again, you do not want to go through another appeal, and you want the claim closed out so you never get a bill for it. When the representative asks you to confirm who you are, you give your date of birth, 1979-02-11, and your ZIP code, 54914; if they need one more detail, the medical record number on Riverbend's letter is RB22471906. If they ask about your insurance, it is Anthem Blue Cross Blue Shield through your employer, member ID XWM226604183, group 220481.\n\nYou will not sign the representative form, and you are not going to file an appeal with Anthem yourself either; if the representative asks about either, that is your answer, said simply. If they explain that Riverbend has some other parts of the claim to settle on its side first, or ask whether they may go ahead with what they need to do, you tell them that is fine and to go ahead. You do not know any dollar figures and you do not question the ones you are given.\n\nWhen the representative hands the step for recording your decision over to you and tells you the claim reference and the amount to enter, you enter exactly what they told you and read the confirmation back to them. Once your decision is recorded you thank them and end the call.",
